# AcadeMY safe development

These instructions apply to every Cursor Agent session in this repository.

## PRESERVE EXISTING BEHAVIOR

When implementing a requested change:

- Change only what is necessary
- Preserve unrelated working functionality
- Avoid large rewrites for small fixes
- Prefer minimal targeted patches
- Do not remove functionality unless explicitly requested
- Do not modify unrelated content
- Do not rename public routes, database fields, RPCs, environment variables, or APIs without proving all consumers have been updated

## INVESTIGATE BEFORE EDITING

Before meaningful multi-file changes:

1. Inspect the existing implementation
2. Trace dependencies and callers
3. Inspect relevant tests
4. Understand routing, data, and auth impact
5. Create a small implementation plan

Do not guess architecture.

## PROTECT WORKING FEATURES

Treat the following as regression-critical:

- Authentication (sign in/out, `/auth/callback`, session cookie `academy-auth-v1`, password reset, guest mode)
- Admin access (`/admin`, `/admin/login`, `hasAdministratorRole`, RPC `is_admin`)
- Routing (`src/routes/`, `src/routeTree.gen.ts`)
- PWA (`public/site.webmanifest`, `src/lib/pwa-register.ts`, `/sw.js`)
- Mobile responsiveness and flashcard 3D / `backface-visibility`
- Supabase integration (`VITE_SUPABASE_*` in browser; `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` only in `*.server.ts`)
- Quiz progress, XP, leaderboard, flashcards, mind maps
- Curriculum content

## DO NOT HIDE FAILURES

Never:

- Delete failing tests merely to obtain a green build
- Weaken assertions without justification
- Suppress TypeScript errors using unsafe casts purely to make compilation pass
- Disable lint, test, or build steps because they fail
- Claim something was tested when it was not

Fix the underlying cause.

## VERIFY AFTER EDITING

After meaningful application changes, automatically use the `academy-guardian` subagent before claiming the task is complete.

Use only these repository commands (do not invent others):

- `npm run verify` — `tsc --noEmit` + `vitest run`. Guardian compares failures to the exact recorded baseline in `.cursor/agents/academy-guardian.md`. Any unmatched failure is a NEW REGRESSION. Do not delete baseline tests.
- `npx eslint <changed-files>` — lint only the files you changed. `npm run lint` (`eslint .`) is a known-red Prettier baseline; do not rewrite the repo to make it green
- `npx vitest run --config vitest.auth.config.ts` — when auth files changed (`-auth-login.integration.tsx` is not in `npm test`)
- `npm run build` then `npm run verify:notes-bundle` — when app, routing, PWA, Vite, Wrangler, or Cloudflare scripts changed

Playwright is not installed. Do not claim live browser, PWA install, or visual breakpoint coverage.

If Guardian returns FAIL:

- Do not declare the task complete
- Diagnose the regression
- Make the minimum necessary correction
- Invoke Guardian again

Completion requires Guardian PASS, except when something requires manual user verification. In that case clearly mark it UNVERIFIED.

## GIT SAFETY

Before editing:

- Inspect `git status`
- Preserve unrelated user changes

After editing:

- Inspect `git diff`
- Report changed files

Never automatically:

- Force push
- `reset --hard`
- Discard unrelated user changes
- Overwrite existing uncommitted work
- Push or deploy unless explicitly requested

## CONTENT SAFETY

Educational content and UI code are different scopes.

If a request concerns animation, layout, responsive design, styling, or components:

DO NOT alter Chemistry / Science / History / Geography / BM / Math educational wording or dataset contents unless explicitly requested.

If content files change unexpectedly, Guardian should fail the review.
